					<p class="body1" align="left"><span class="body1 style73"> <h2>News archive</h2><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-02-21 | Wednesday</font></strong><br><br><img src="http://www.thestranger.com/binary/caab/musicfollow1-160.jpg" alt="" width="160" height="360" /><br /><br />Look, i&#39;m not playin. Us Massliners really <em>are</em> everywhere. Another case in point: Massline forum member/restauranteur/injera pusher <strong>Rawita</strong> aka <strong>Rahwa Habte</strong> (left) is featured in this week&#39;s <strong>Stranger</strong>, calling her (and her sister <strong>Asmeret</strong>) restaurant, <strong>Hidmo</strong>, a <em>hip hop mecca</em>. Peep out the article <a href="http://www.thestranger.com/seattle/Content?oid=161460">here</a>, and come thru to Hidmo <a href="../smf/index.php?topic=1148.0">this Friday night</a>, as <strong>Sabzi</strong> and myself will be spinning the cuts for y&#39;all. You might need a band aid for all them cuts! Shout out to Charles Mudede for the article.<p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-02-21 | Wednesday</font></strong><br><br>Six degrees of Massline: There&#39;s no <strong>Kevin Bacon</strong> involved in this, but as some of you know, comedian <strong>Hari Kondabolu</strong> was on <em>Jimmy Kimmel Live!</em> last Monday night. You see, he&#39;s connected to Massline because he done did a Massline-sponsored comedy show in January (hosted by <strong>Sabzi</strong> and <strong>Khingz</strong>), wrote and starred in a film short directed by Sabzi&#39;s brother <strong>Zia</strong>, and brands his own comedy with responsible social commentary that is parallel to what Massline is all about.<br /><br />The other connection this week comes from rival network NBC. Massline board member <strong>HAUNT</strong> - who did separate flyers for January&#39;s <strong>Common Market</strong> and <strong>Blue Scholars</strong> shows - appeared on <em>Conan O&#39;Brien</em> last week with his girlfriend for a Valentine&#39;s Day sketch:<br /><br /><br /><br /><br /><object width="425" height="350" type="application/x-shockwave-flash" data="http://www.youtube.com/v/4ynn_rHJhl0"><br /><param name="movie" value="http://www.youtube.com/v/4ynn_rHJhl0"></param><br /><param name="wmode" value="transparent"></param><br /></object><br /><br /><br />Watch out y&#39;all, us Massliners are everywhere!<br />Peace<br />dj daps1<br /> <p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-02-20 | Tuesday</font></strong><br><br>Bay Area / West Koast stand up!!! More dates for the <strong>Stop the Killings Tour</strong> to be announced in the near future.<br /><br /><img src="http://i12.tinypic.com/2yocn5k.jpg" alt="" width="361" height="478" /><br /><br /><img src="http://i15.tinypic.com/42o18vn.jpg" alt="" width="360" height="479" /><br /><br />It&#39;s also Tuesday, which means a short work/school week, which means we&#39;re gettin&#39; closer to the <strong>Lovework CD Release Party</strong>! Info on the show listed on the right hand side. Here&#39;s the flyer if you&#39;ve been living under a boulder (or if you&#39;re from <strong>Boulder</strong> and you have no idea what of what i&#39;m talkin about):<br /><br /><img src="http://a56.ac-images.myspacecdn.com/images01/28/l_dcdb5d3752cadc04933f13e768bf8887.jpg" alt="" width="275" height="361" /><br /><br />We also would like to give a big shout out to our fellow funny dude and Massline supporter, comedian <a href="http://youtube.com/results?search_query=hari+kondabolu&amp;search=Search">Hari Kondabolu</a>, who appeared on last night&#39;s <em>Jimmy Kimmel Live!</em> Congratulations!<br /><br />peace<br />dj daps1<p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-02-19 | Monday</font></strong><br><br><img src="http://farm1.static.flickr.com/145/395612237_08cbce89c6.jpg?v=0" alt="" width="430" height="323" /><br /><br />HAPPY BORN DAY TO YOUR EMCEES FAVORITE EMCEE, GEOLOGIC! Give him a shout out <strong><a href="../smf/index.php?topic=1143.0">here</a></strong><a href="../smf/index.php?topic=1143.0">.</a><br /><em><br /></em>Peace<br />dj daps1<em><br /><br />Photo taken by me in July of 2003 for the Wing Luke Asian Museum&#39;s hip hop exhibit.</em> <p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-02-19 | Monday</font></strong><br><br>happy monday all.<br /><br />today is an important day, folkers.&nbsp; because it&#39;s president&#39;s day? <br /><br />HAHAHAHAHAHAHAHA.<br /><br /><br />no.<br /><br />actually, there&#39;s a few things goin on.&nbsp; for those who had the fortunate opportunity of attending the <strong>MASSLINE Presents: Stand Up Comedy!</strong> show, you will remember our good friend <strong>Hari Kondabolu</strong>.&nbsp; well, tonight <strong>Hari</strong> will be featuring on the late <strong>Jimmy Kimmel</strong> show.&nbsp; so, if you&#39;re up that late, tune in and support our fellow Seattlite speak some truth on national television.<br /><br />many ups that are &quot;big&quot; in nature go to our <strong>206 Zulu</strong> homies.&nbsp; from the showcase that was at the Sundiata Festival to the extensive line up at Neumo&#39;s shortly after, the local Zulu chapter put in hella work this past weekend to see that hip hop was represented substantially.<br /><br />the countdown to the release of <strong>Gabriel Teodros&#39; &quot;Lovework&quot;</strong> is nearing its end.&nbsp; i&#39;ll tell you that i&#39;m pumped like a pair of mid-90&#39;s Reebok sneakers.<br /><br />yessir.<br /><br />saba<p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><center><div class="pagenumbers"><A HREF="archive.php?from=210">[&lt;&lt;]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=0">[1]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=5">[2]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=10">[3]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=15">[4]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=20">[5]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=25">[6]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=30">[7]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=35">[8]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=40">[9]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=45">[10]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=50">[11]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=55">[12]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=60">[13]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=65">[14]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=70">[15]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=75">[16]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=80">[17]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=85">[18]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=90">[19]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=95">[20]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=100">[21]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=105">[22]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=110">[23]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=115">[24]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=120">[25]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=125">[26]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=130">[27]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=135">[28]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=140">[29]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=145">[30]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=150">[31]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=155">[32]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=160">[33]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=165">[34]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=170">[35]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=175">[36]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=180">[37]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=185">[38]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=190">[39]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=195">[40]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=200">[41]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=205">[42]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=210">[43]</A> [44] <A HREF="archive.php?from=220">[45]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=225">[46]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=230">[47]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=235">[48]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=240">[49]</A> <A HREF="archive